[2026-02-03T09:55:02.618593] BFS Analysis:
- Strict level-order dependency: level L must complete before L+1 starts
- Within a level: neighbor discovery can be parallelized
- Output order: must match sequential (queue FIFO order within each level)
- Strategy: Level-synchronized parallel BFS
  - Process current frontier in parallel
  - Each thread discovers neighbors, writes to thread-local next-level buffer
  - Merge buffers in fixed order (by thread ID) to preserve determinism
  - Deduplicate visited nodes with atomic flags or critical section
- Rejected: fully async task-based (non-deterministic ordering), single-level parallelism only (limited speedup on deep graphs)
- Best fit: OpenMP with explicit barriers between levels
